{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And the sense of 'and you shall place it upon a cord of tekhelet.'</b> With a cord of tekhelet, for the tzitz was tied on two sides. There is no doubt that the face of the mitznefet is at the place of the forehead, not on the head, and elsewhere it is written 'and they shall place upon it a cord of tekhelet' (below 39:31), to place upon the mitznefet at the place of the forehead. Do not wonder at the word עַל, for like it: 'and the men came upon the women' (below 35:22), 'a wave-offering upon the bread of first-fruits before YHWH' (Leviticus 23:20), 'upon two lambs' (ibid.), 'the fat upon the breast' (ibid. 7:30), and many like these. Now you will never find otherwise, for the mitznefet was only for Aaron alone, and the migba'ot for his sons. Some say that migba'ot is from the root of גִּבְעוֹת (Genesis 49:26), for the mitznefet crowns the head and wraps it, and likewise it is written צְנֹף יְצַנְפְךָ צְנֵפָה (Isaiah 22:18), and וְעֹטְךָ עָטָה (ibid. 22:17). One who knows the manner of wrapping the mitznefet will know its meaning — not this: 'the low high, and the high low' (Ezekiel 21:31), for it is a craft. Now it is written 'and you shall place the mitznefet on his head, and you shall place the nezer of holiness upon the mitznefet' (below 29:6), and the tzitz is called nezer, and like it: 'and upon him shall the nezer blossom' (Psalms 132:18) — perhaps all is from the root of ציץ, it appears, and thus מַצְיִץ מִן הַחֲרַכִּים (Song of Songs 2:9). Know that in the two openings that are in the brain at the forehead, there the force of the five senses converges, and there the faculty of imagination, and there thought begins. Therefore it is written of the tzitz 'to bear the iniquity of the holy things' — perhaps the thought of those who consecrate was not proper."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The citation '(למטה לה כב)' refers to Exodus 35:22; 'למטה' meaning later in the same book of Exodus."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:01.484501662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}